startLine: 1
endLine: 40
content: "1: # System prompt - typical case\n2: \n3: This is the exact text the frontend sends as the `system` argument of\n4: `send_chat_message` in this scenario. It is built by:\n5: \n6: 1. `composeSystemWithLanguage(base, force, language, rules)` in\n7:    `src/lib/response-language.ts`.\n8: 2. `composeAgentSystem(agent, skillContexts, loadedSkills)` in\n9:    `src/lib/agent-system.ts`.\n10: \n11: Inputs:\n12: \n13: - `agent.id` = `build`\n14: - `agent.skills` = `[{ kind: \"global\", id: \"code-review\" }]`\n15: - `agent.personality` (full text below)\n16: - `skillContexts` has one global skill (`code-review`) and one local\n17:   skill (`commit`)\n18: - `loadedSkillNames` = `[]` (turn 1, nothing loaded yet)\n19: - `forceResponseLanguage` = `false`\n20: - `responseLanguage` = `\"en\"`\n21: - `rules` = `\"\"` (no AGENTS.md content)\n22: \n23: The final `system` string the LLM receives is:\n24: \n25: ```\n26: # 1. Agent flow\n27: \n28: Follow system sections in order. Each numbered block maps to a phase of the reply.\n29: Turn 1: batch-load every agent-bound skill with the `skill` tool. No prose.\n30: Then load matching workspace skills with `skill` when they are listed and relevant.\n31: Call only tools in the request tools list (local and MCP). Do not invent names.\n32: Finally answer using the agent personality at the end of this system prompt.\n33: \n34: # 2. Agent skill loading - turn 1\n35: \n36: Single tool batch, exactly 1 `skill` call, before any other tool or prose:\n37: \n38: 1. `code-review`\n39: \n40: No other tool calls on turn 1. Retry a failed skill once; report on turn 2.\n\n(Showing lines 1-40 of 280. Use offset=41 to continue.)"